### Attempt SQL injection through patient creation
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pet_name": "X' OR 1=1--",
  "species": "Cat",
  "breed": "Test",
  "dob": "2024-01-14",
  "gender": "Female",
  "neutered_spayed": true,
  "owner_name": "Security Test",
  "email": "security-test@example.com",
  "phone": "0822223344"
}

### Attempt reflected/script content in an owner name
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json
X-CSRF-Token: obtain-from-GET-api-csrf-token

{
  "pet_name": "Luna",
  "species": "Cat",
  "breed": "Test",
  "dob": "2024-01-14",
  "gender": "Female",
  "neutered_spayed": true,
  "owner_name": "<script>alert(1)</script>",
  "email": "security-test@example.com",
  "phone": "0822223344"
}

### Request a CSRF token
GET http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/csrf-token

### Reject a patient-changing request with no CSRF token
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/patients
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "pet_name": "NoCsrf",
  "species": "Dog",
  "breed": "Test",
  "dob": "2024-01-14",
  "gender": "Male",
  "neutered_spayed": false,
  "owner_name": "Security Test",
  "email": "nocrsf@example.com",
  "phone": "0822223344"
}

### Reject an invalid upload content type
POST http://127.0.0.1:5000/api/uploads
Content-Type: multipart/form-data; boundary=securityBoundary
X-CSRF-Token: obtain-from-GET-api-csrf-token

--securityBoundary
Content-Disposition: form-data; name="photo"; filename="report.txt"
Content-Type: text/plain

not an image
--securityBoundary--
